  "definitionSource": "TypeScript ProjectionBuilderFor: root From ItemAdded usingCompositeKey, children identifiedBy id with From ItemAdded usingCompositeKey/usingParentCompositeKey, and child Join ItemNamed on id using the same content/Subject/event-source-id/constant expressions. See when_matching_kernel_fixtures.spec.ts. Unlike a root join, the child join resolves its custom key. Chronicle 19.26.2 uses the resolved child-join key as both the root document key and the child identifier, so a child join only updates children whose root has the same identifier (https://github.com/Cratis/Chronicle/issues/4530). Children are created through the `$value` parent-key shortcut; this fixture isolates child-join key evaluation, not parent resolution. Root and child identifiers deliberately coincide; this proves custom-key evaluation and live updates, not arbitrary parent lookup or persistent-sink placement. The in-memory join replaces the matched root state with its join changes, dropping title and __initialized; the untouched subject's root remains unchanged. This is a Chronicle in-memory sink bug: root properties and sibling children are dropped (https://github.com/Cratis/Chronicle/issues/4531), so in-memory results can differ from persistent storage. ReadModelScenario rejects composite identifiers and child joins.",
